;; clj-kondo configuration for {{project-name}}.
;;
;; This file exists even when empty, and that is deliberate. clj-kondo's
;; --copy-configs step — which is how a dependency's exported linter config
;; reaches this project — prints
;;
;;   No configs copied because config dir (.clj-kondo) does not exist.
;;
;; and exits 0 when this directory is absent. A generated project had no
;; .clj-kondo/, so the import silently did nothing and the Wagoe registry
;; macros (defworkflow, defsearch, defreport, defevent, defpush) kept linting
;; as unresolved symbols (BOU-503).
;;
;; Run `bb lint:imports` once, and again after changing dependencies. It
;; populates .clj-kondo/imports/, which is committed alongside this file.
;;
;; Project-specific linter settings go here.
